{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Abram heeded the voice of Sarai.</b> Scripture does not say \"and he did so,\" but rather that he heeded the voice of Sarai, to hint that even though Abram greatly desired children, he did not do so without Sarai's permission. Moreover, even now his intention was not that he himself would build a family through Hagar and that his seed would come from her; rather, his entire intention was to fulfill the will of Sarah, that she might build a family through her, so that she would have gratification through the children of her maidservant, or that she herself might thereby merit children — as our Sages say (Genesis Rabbah 42:2). And Scripture further states \"and Sarai took,\" to inform us that Abram did not rush into the matter until Sarai took her and placed her in his bosom. And Scripture mentions \"Sarai Abram's wife,\" \"to Abram her husband,\" to hint that Sarah did not despair of Abram and did not distance herself from him, for she is his wife and he is her husband; rather, she wanted Hagar too to become his wife. Therefore it says \"to him for a wife,\" that she should not be as a concubine but as a married wife to him. All of this reflects Sarah's discipline and the honor she accorded her husband."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:29:55.297345410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}